### User Management API - CRUD Operations Test Suite
### Make sure your API is running on http://localhost:5171
### Execute requests one by one to see the complete CRUD workflow

# Test 1: Get all users (should return initial 3 users)
GET http://localhost:5171/api/users
Accept: application/json

###

# Test 2: Get user by ID (should return John Doe)
GET http://localhost:5171/api/users/1
Accept: application/json

###

# Test 3: Get user by ID (should return Jane Smith)
GET http://localhost:5171/api/users/2
Accept: application/json

###

# Test 4: Get user by ID (should return Bob Johnson)
GET http://localhost:5171/api/users/3
Accept: application/json

###

# Test 5: Create a new user (should return 201 Created)
POST http://localhost:5171/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Johnson"
}

###

# Test 6: Create another new user (should return 201 Created)
POST http://localhost:5171/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Charlie Brown"
}

###

# Test 7: Get all users again (should now show 5 users)
GET http://localhost:5171/api/users
Accept: application/json

###

# Test 8: Update an existing user (should return 200 OK)
PUT http://localhost:5171/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe Updated"
}

###

# Test 9: Get the updated user to verify changes
GET http://localhost:5171/api/users/1
Accept: application/json

###

# Test 10: Delete a user (should return 204 No Content)
DELETE http://localhost:5171/api/users/2

###

# Test 11: Try to get the deleted user (should return 404 Not Found)
GET http://localhost:5171/api/users/2
Accept: application/json

###

# Test 12: Get all users to verify deletion
GET http://localhost:5171/api/users
Accept: application/json

###

# Test 13: Try to get a non-existent user (should return 404)
GET http://localhost:5171/api/users/999
Accept: application/json

###

# Test 14: Try to update a non-existent user (should return 404)
PUT http://localhost:5171/api/users/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Non-existent User"
}

###

# Test 15: Try to delete a non-existent user (should return 404)
DELETE http://localhost:5171/api/users/999

###

# Test 16: Create user with empty name (should return 400 Bad Request)
POST http://localhost:5171/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": ""
}

###

# Test 17: Update user with empty name (should return 400 Bad Request)
PUT http://localhost:5171/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": ""
}